# The engine commit that the example-validation gate builds `paged-inspect`
# from (briefing §6.2 / §7 "docs version to the renderer's minor version").
# Format: a single commit SHA on the first non-comment line.
#
# REPOSITORY: since 2026-10-18 the engine lives in the monorepo paged-media/paged
# at engine/core, and this pin names a paged-media/paged commit (the gates check
# it out and build `core/engine/core`). The release tags v0.N.P were carried
# over to the monorepo. The "tag commit" values in the history below, from
# v0.73.3 back, name commits of the archived paged-media/core repository
# (v0.73.4 was 8eb9e21 there).
#
# PIN POLICY: this pin tracks the LATEST core RELEASE TAG, not core@main. Bump it
# to the new tag's commit on every core release (e.g. v0.35.0 → the commit
# `git -C paged rev-list -n1 v0.35.0` resolves to), via a deliberate PR. This keeps
# the docs gate building paged-inspect from the exact engine the published
# @paged-media packages ship from — so a validated example is one a released
# renderer accepts, never a main-only or pre-release one. The weekly core-drift job
# may surface a newer green main, but the pin only moves when a release is cut.
#
# Currently: v0.73.4 (tag commit 9408270). A patch on protocol 73: a
# keep that moves a note's reference, verified against InDesign (C-45); a
# cross-reference's chapter number and live captions print live (L-09);
# tagged PDF elements named after their paragraph style, its PDF export tag
# as the role (ADR 182); A-33 complete (ADR 183); and the IDML adapter's
# tracked-insertion edits, buttons and multi-state objects kept on save, and
# caption providers and export tags read. All four packages answer at 0.73.4
# on the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.73.3 (tag commit a8dce53). A patch on protocol 73
# (v0.73.2, the zip 9 security update, was released while this pin stayed
# put): nested tables drawn as tables and rows that fit the text area (ADRs
# 176, 177); a story that grows a page for its footnotes and continues a note
# where it stopped, and each chain frame setting lines at its own measure
# (ADRs 178, 179); the viewer opens a .paged container from its model part
# (ADR 181); Create Tagged PDF (ADR 182); an IDML save that drops a removed
# page's spread and states a blank document's setup (ADR 183); and the
# `paged package` command. All four packages answer at 0.73.3 on the registry
# (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.73.1 (tag commit 7a257bb). Additive on protocol 73: a table
# row's Start Row option moves it and the rows after it as a paragraph's
# StartParagraph moves its first line, asked of InDesign (ADR 175); the
# rowStartRow / rowKeepWithNext paths reach a row through any of its cells.
# All four packages answer at 0.73.1 on the registry (`latest`), checked
# before this pin moved.
#
# v0.73.0 (tag commit 4114445). Protocol 73: endnotes inserted,
# deleted and converted from footnotes as InDesign does it (ADR 174). The first
# endnote of a document makes the endnote story on a page of its own, in an
# endnote frame over the margin box; a new note's range goes after the range of
# the reference before it; a footnote converts to an endnote of its text in one
# undo step; the endnotes collection reads. All four packages answer at 0.73.0
# on the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.72.0 (tag commit 9d5d184). Protocol 72: generated text,
# editorial notes and bookmarks over the wire. Generate Index writes the index as
# InDesign does (ADR 168); a cross-reference prints its destination's page live
# and Update Cross-References rewrites its text from its format (ADR 169);
# endnotes are read and numbered as InDesign numbers them (ADR 170); PDF export
# writes the document's bookmarks as a nested outline (ADR 171); an editorial
# note is one character of the text that prints nothing, and notes are inserted,
# edited, deleted and converted to text (ADR 172); bookmarks are created,
# renamed, moved and deleted (ADR 173). All four packages answer at 0.72.0 on the
# registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.71.13 (tag commit c6f329e). The canvas worker and the viewer
# session no longer hold themselves across an await (a timer landing in a GPU
# wait crashed them); a rotated frame, group or placed image scales along its own
# axes; a picture without a transform is clipped to its frame, as InDesign does;
# a committed change reports what it changed (a handle resize's reflow, a
# script's writes and pages, a page's origin in its spread, a table's header and
# footer bands; ADR 159, additive). IDML export keeps next/previous page numbers,
# replaced tables, re-poured cells and text typed into empty or new paragraphs,
# and writes crops in InDesign's convention. Protocol 71. All four packages
# answer at 0.71.13 on the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.71.12 (tag commit ee5d9bf). Footnotes as InDesign sets them:
# numbered through each story with page/spread/section restarts and prefix and
# suffix (ADR 156), under each column or across the frame (ADR 160), and a note
# too tall for its frame continued in the next under the continuing rule or its
# reference line moved on (ADR 161). Every page-number style InDesign offers
# (ADR 157), multi-level lists (ADR 158), column rules (ADR 155), placed PDFs
# drawn from their own operations (ADR 154), and seven additive catalog paths
# (line setting, no-break, list level). Protocol 71. All four packages answer
# at 0.71.12 on the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
# (v0.71.11 was released while this pin stayed put.)
#
# v0.71.10 (tag commit d52ae6a). The GPU lane held to the CPU lane
# (ADR 146): drop shadows share one stamp set, the page isolation layer is
# bounded by what the page paints, dashed strokes and gradient feathers draw on
# Vello, and a CPU-vs-Vello parity gate runs hard on every core push. A rotated
# frame's gradient default as InDesign sets it (ADR 147), canned Wavy strokes,
# and dashes laid out side by side as InDesign fits them (ADR 148). No wire or
# catalog change; protocol 71. All four packages answer at 0.71.10 on the
# registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.71.9 (tag commit 3e77f36). Exact positions (leading and glyph
# advances summed exactly, rounded once), text wrap as InDesign sets it
# (jump-object and next-column wraps, the ragged breaker beside a wrap, contour
# written `Contour`), the composer's line allowance and a hyphenation zone that
# no longer widens word spaces, and condition sets that record each condition's
# visibility. No wire change; protocol 71. All four packages answer at 0.71.9 on
# the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.71.7 (tag commit ad571c7). The core parity campaign's first
# release: every rule asked of InDesign 20.0.1 and gated against its PDF.
# Justified last lines and the binding side, gradients and tints, conditional
# text, stored TOC text, tracked deletions and button states, tables and
# footnote references as characters of their line, nested/line/GREP styles and
# OpenType features, transparency per fill/stroke/content with group isolation
# and knockout, and a PDF export whose text is real text. Additive catalog
# paths only; protocol 71. All four packages answer at 0.71.7 on the registry
# (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.71.5 (tag commit 921a99a). Placed images: an image-free frame
# no longer blanks every placed image after it on the GPU canvas; a frame that
# names FillProportionally covers itself at one uniform scale instead of
# stretching, in the render, `paged place --fit` and the IDML export alike; a
# colour written as a swatch address is stored as the swatch id. Includes
# v0.71.4 (e609b5a). No wire change. All four packages answer at 0.71.5 on the
# registry (`latest`).
#
# v0.71.3 (tag commit a7d6684). Catalog only: each typed property
# schema names the IDML element and attribute it stands for (355 of 403 rows),
# which the IDML element reference (idml.paged.media/reference/) reads to show
# an attribute's type, values and paged.set path. No wire change. All four
# packages answer at 0.71.3 on the registry (`latest`).
#
# v0.71.2 (tag commit 7cad959). A patch on v0.71.1: a caret is an
# address (`storyRange:<story>@n..n` names the paragraph it stands in, for
# reads and writes), which the object-model panels need whenever nothing is
# selected. No wire or catalog change. All four packages answer at 0.71.2 on
# the registry (`latest`).
#
# v0.71.1 (tag commit 6adb3b7). Protocol 71, the object model
# (ADRs 131, 132): one address grammar for every object, typed property schemas,
# `Set` / `RequestGet` / `RequestQuery` on the wire, typed commands (`paged
# invoke`, `paged ops` on the CLI; `paged.invoke` in scripts), text variables
# created and instanced, and the Boa host-object bridge. v0.71.1 re-pins the IDML
# adapter so the export follows the model (Visible/Locked, authored text
# variables, page-item names). All four packages answer at 0.71.1 on the
# registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved; core's own CI was green on
# v0.71.0.
#
# v0.70.2 (tag commit c7a4b78). A renderer patch on v0.70.1:
# rectangles and text frames cast their object shadow from what they paint (a
# stroke-only frame from its stroke, a stroked frame pushed out by the stroke's
# outer part, a rounded frame along its corners, text in an unfilled frame),
# measured against InDesign 2025. No wire change. All four packages answer at
# 0.70.2 on the registry (`latest`).
#
# v0.70.1 (tag commit 172d652). A renderer patch on v0.70.0: an
# oval's or polygon's object shadow is cast from what it paints (an unfilled
# shape from its stroke; a stroked oval as an ellipse with the stroke's outer
# half), measured against InDesign 2025. No wire change. All four packages
# answer at 0.70.1 on the registry (`latest`).
#
# v0.70.0 (tag commit 9bc22c2). Two protocol versions on from
# v0.68.0. Protocol 69 (v0.69.0, the data-publishing batch): fields at the
# caret, document-scoped plugin labels (`setDocumentMetadata`), pages a merge
# can make. Protocol 70: pages and masters for presentations (`movePage`,
# `setPageMetadata`, page links, snapshots without items, master editing and
# create/delete/rename; ADR 129) and the platform doors for plugin content
# (scene-layer scoped fonts, a handle on every batch mint, drop shadows on
# every shape; ADR 130). All four packages (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk,
# idml-viewer) answer at 0.70.0 on the registry (`latest`), checked before this
# pin moved; core's own CI was green on the tag commit.
#
# v0.68.0 (tag commit c7c16a7). Two protocol versions on from
# v0.66.0 (v0.67.0 was released while this pin stayed put). Protocol 67 moves
# snapping into the engine (requestSnapPoint, setSnapSettings; ADR 125).
# Protocol 68 draws scene-layer text in its own face: a run's family plus
# weight/italic resolve through the host-registered fonts, the default face only
# as a fallback, reported on the reply as `fontFallbacks` (ADR 126). All four
# packages (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at 0.68.0 on
# the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.66.0 (tag commit fcffd2d). Two protocol versions on from v0.64.0
# (v0.65.0 was released while this pin stayed put). Protocol 65 widened the
# write surface: duplicateElements, stroke alignment and effects on every kind
# that draws them, opacity and blend on groups, paragraphComposer, a style's
# settable properties and a story's grow rule readable. Protocol 66 adds a pen
# path's end cap and line ends, the gradient axis read back on paths and ovals,
# rotate/scale/shear about a given point, a text frame's glyphs as outlines,
# plugin metadata on every scene-tree node, binary scene images and part bytes,
# `DeletePagedPart`, `deleteTable`, exact table undo, and per-page scene
# invalidation. All four packages (canvas-wasm,
# introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at 0.66.0 on the registry (`latest`),
# checked before this pin moved; core's own CI was green on the tag commit.
#
# v0.64.0 (tag commit 6dea692): protocol 64 makes a batch of attributes the
# model already carried SETTABLE on the wire: `setFlowGrowRule` (a story's frame chain may grow, ADR 026, with
# copyFrameOptions per ADR 029), keep options and StartParagraph (the
# break-before rule, ADR 028), span and split columns (SpanColumnType), and the
# list-marker attributes. Rendering also moved: forced line breaks (U+2028),
# list-marker placement and character styles, text-frame StrokeAlignment insets.
# All four packages (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at
# 0.64.0 on the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved. NOTE core's
# own `ci` was red at the tag (its pdf export-diff lane, on the new list
# fixtures) — a CI-only lane, not a shipped-package defect; core main is green
# again after it.
#
# v0.63.0 made the SCRIPT BUDGET a wire parameter: `ExecuteScript` carries
# an optional `ScriptBudgetWire`, absent meaning the engine's own ceilings (the
# editor's 2 s REPL guard, unchanged) and `wallClockMs: 0` meaning no deadline.
#
# v0.63.0 also carries two fixes the docs gate cares about: `paged.set(id,
# "itemLayer", …)` actually WRITES now (protocol 62 taught the catalog to parse
# the path and the wire to apply it, and never taught `js_value_to_wire` it was
# string-valued, so it returned false and wrote nothing — a806321), and the
# directional feather paints the real coverage mask shared with the PDF lane
# rather than stamping a white blurred path (72cd7b3).
#
# v0.62.0 added `itemLayer` (assign an EXISTING page item to a layer — until
# protocol 62 layer membership was birth-only, settable in a paged-gen fixture
# and nowhere else), `UnlinkFrames.restore_target`, and the render-effect
# sweep's fixes: eleven operations that the wire accepted and reported success
# for while changing nothing on the page.
#
# Why the policy says "a tag whose packages are PUBLISHED", not just "a tag":
# the pin once named v0.51.2, a tag that was cut but never shipped — its release,
# and v0.51.1 and v0.51.0 before it, all died on an expired NPM_TOKEN that npm
# reported as a 404. The gate was then building paged-inspect from an engine no
# published package shipped from, which is exactly what this pin exists to prevent.
# v0.61.0 ended that gap; v0.63.0 is verified the same way — all four packages
# (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at 0.63.0 on the
# registry. Check that before moving this pin, not after. NOTE the v0.63.0
# publish took two attempts: the first was stopped by core's own subset audit
# because `paged-sdk` had come to link `paged-mutate` transitively, and npm
# answered PUT 202 (queued) rather than 200 for two of the four packages, so
# they read 0.62.0 for a few minutes after a green run. Both are reasons to
# check the registry rather than the workflow's conclusion.
#
# The WebGPU live preview does not build from this commit — it consumes the
# published npm `@paged-media/idml-viewer` at the matching release (its bundled
# wasm), so this pin governs the CI example/scripting gates only.
94082703cf34b96a0fcde034f2f8875962caedc2
